agent	Execute Claude Code CLI	2026-10-21T18:30:54.2426088Z {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFrmX5aN5sHsb6aJARj2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UFdBrLQdbj2eVTibKa6bfv","name":"mcp__safeoutputs__add_comment","input":{"body":"Thanks for the report! This is an automated first-pass triage; a maintainer will make the final call.\n\n**Reproduction:** not attempted: this is a style/option request, and the snippets show current style rather than a malfunction.\n**Assessment:** The current output follows Black's documented wrapping: if a full expression doesn't fit on one line, it is split with the closing bracket on its own line, and a trailing comma is added. The style docs also say that configuration options are \"deliberately limited and rarely added\". A `no-short-lines` / `min-line-length` option would run against that policy. The magic trailing comma is the one rule that takes previous formatting into account, and `--skip-magic-trailing-comma` only removes it. It doesn't produce the compact layout you describe.\n**Next step:** See \"How Black wraps lines\" and \"The magic trailing comma\" in the code style docs (https://black.readthedocs.io/en/stable/the_black_code_style/current_style.html). A maintainer will decide whether such an option fits the project.\n\n<sub>black-issue-triage skill v1.0.0 · suggested for maintainers: `R: not a bug`</sub>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":618,"cache_read_input_tokens":49388,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":618,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":45,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f22e3c08-18d8-423a-9814-b4d1134c31ad","uuid":"a36b0757-33c3-483a-871f-200d481849d1","tim